Highlights: **Webhook signing** is now supported to secure webhook deliveries, and a fix for duplicate emails on retry improves reliability.  
@noor added webhook signing (issue #201).  
@viktor fixed duplicate emails on retry (issue #188).  
BREAKING: The legacy API key header X-Key was removed.  
Upgrade: Migrate to using the new API key header X-API-Key.

Highlights: Version 3.0.0 introduces **role-based access control** and improves configuration flexibility with a new default page size.  
@carla added role-based access control (issue #540).  
@deepak changed the default page size from 50 to 25 (issue #533).  
BREAKING: config files must use YAML instead of JSON.  
Upgrade: Migrate all config files to use YAML format.

Highlights: Fixed a memory leak in the image resizer and added a new health check endpoint. **Health check endpoint** is now available for monitoring service status.  

@yuki fixed a memory leak in the image resizer.  
@tariq added a health check endpoint.  

BREAKING: Python 3.8 is no longer supported. Upgrade: Migrate to Python 3.9 or higher.

Highlights: We've added **bulk user import** for faster onboarding and improved tax report accuracy.  
@anna added bulk user import (issue #1204).  
@rui fixed incorrect totals in the tax report (issue #1190).  
BREAKING: the report_v1 export format was removed.  
Upgrade: Migrate to the new report_v2 export format to continue using reports.

Highlights: Fixed a crash when the config file is empty and changed log output to JSON by default  
@moses fixed a crash when the config file is empty  
@ella changed log output to JSON by default  
BREAKING: the --plain-logs flag was renamed to --text-logs  
Upgrade: If you're using the --plain-logs flag, update your commands to use --text-logs instead

Highlights: Dark mode and keyboard navigation are now available in version 4.1.0  
@hugo added dark mode (issue #902)  
@sana added keyboard shortcuts for navigation (issue #915)  
BREAKING: Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported. Upgrade: Migrate to a modern browser to continue using the application.

Highlights: Version 7.0.0 introduces **S3-compatible object storage** as the default backend and improves startup performance with large plugin sets.  
@pedro improved storage backend support with S3-compatible object storage (issue #2210).  
@mina fixed slow startup with large plugin sets (issue #2198).  

BREAKING: Local disk storage must be migrated before upgrading.  
Upgrade: Migrate local disk storage to a supported backend before upgrading to 7.0.0.

